Q) Can static methods be overloaded?
        Yes. Static methods can be overloaded.
        Static methods can have the same name with different parameter lists.

Example:- class Calculator {
    static void add(int a, int b) {
        System.out.println(a + b);
    }
    static void add(int a, int b, int c) {
        System.out.println(a + b + c);
    }
}

The compiler determines which static method to call based on the parameter list.

Q) Can static methods be overridden?
    No, Static methods cannot be overridden,
    because overriding depends on objects,
    static methods doesn't depends on objects
    Hence, Static Methods can't be overridden.

Q) Can final methods be overloaded?
    Yes, Final methods can be overloaded.
 it can have overloaded versions with different parameter lists.

